    "steps": [
      {
        "text": "Scatter the ginger, garlic and onion over the bottom of a wide, non-reactive pan. Lay the bangus on top in one layer and tuck the eggplant and bitter gourd around it.",
        "minutes": null
      },
      {
        "text": "Pour in the vinegar and water. Add the peppercorns, salt, fish sauce and chilies.",
        "minutes": null
      },
      {
        "text": "Bring to a boil over medium heat, uncovered and <strong>without stirring</strong>, so the raw edge of the vinegar cooks off.",
        "minutes": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Cover, lower the heat and simmer until the fish is cooked through and the vegetables are tender.",
        "minutes": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "Drizzle in the oil and simmer a few minutes more. Taste the sauce and add salt if needed. Shake the pan instead of stirring so the fish stays whole.",
        "minutes": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Serve hot or at room temperature with rice and plenty of the sauce.",
        "minutes": null
      }
    ],
    "tips": "Paksiw keeps 3 days in the fridge. Reheat it gently in its sauce, and leave out the bitter gourd if your household does not like it."
